course: dictionary
lesson: 6417
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The kingdom of God is like a tiny mustard seed» is about a seed, not a sauce.
explain: Look at what the word does in the sentence. In «The curtains were mustard», mustard is a colour, because curtains can be a colour. Ask yourself: is this word a thing, a colour, or an action? That clue often points to the right meaning.
explain: Some words belong to phrases, and a phrase can mean something different from its single words. «Keen as mustard» does not mean something yellow is eager. It is an informal way of saying someone is very eager. When you meet a phrase you do not understand, look at the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant.
fact: Mustard can be a paste or sauce, a plant, a colour, or part of a phrase.
fact: «Keen as mustard» is an informal phrase (UK) that means very eager.
fact: «Cut the mustard» is informal and means be good enough.
fact: The parable of the mustard seed says the kingdom of God grows from something tiny into something big.
exercise: «The kingdom of God is like a tiny mustard seed that grows into a large plant.» What is the mustard in this sentence? | A dark yellow colour | A hot yellow sauce for hot dogs | A kind of bird | *The seed of the mustard plant
exercise: Maya says, «Ravi is keen as mustard about the football match.» What does keen as mustard mean? | Good enough to play | *Very eager | Covered in yellow paint | Cross and grumpy
exercise: «The curtains were mustard, a dark yellow.» What colour are the curtains? | Blue-green | *Dark yellow | Pale white | Bright red
test: Ben's drawing did not cut the mustard, his teacher said. What does cut the mustard mean? | Was painted yellow | Was finished very early | Was too big to fit on the wall | *Was not good enough
test: «Mustard or egg yolk helps oil droplets stay apart longer in a dressing.» Which meaning of mustard is used here? | A small yellow flower | A phrase that means eager | A dark yellow colour | *A paste or sauce made from mustard seeds
exam: Which phrase means very eager? | English mustard | *Keen as mustard | Mustard seed | Cut the mustard
